fn resume_offset(state: &UploadState) -> u64 {
    let acked = state.last_chunk_index;
    acked * state.chunk_size
}

last_chunk_index gets set when we start sending a chunk, not when the server acks it

That's the bug. `last_chunk_index` is set at send time, so after an interruption it points at a chunk the server may not have confirmed. If the server did get it, you resend it as a duplicate, and if it didn't, the math is still wrong. Resume from the acknowledged count instead:

rust
fn resume_offset(state: &UploadState) -> u64 {
    // next byte after the last chunk the server confirmed
    state.acked_chunks as u64 * state.chunk_size
}


This assumes you have or add an `acked_chunks` field that's only incremented on a successful ack response. Want me to wire that into the send loop too?

